      "Choosing the initial discontinuity location as zero is a coordinate convention, expressed as 'say x = 0' [printed p. 5, Section 1.2.1, opening paragraph].",
      "A medium discontinuity concerns material properties, in distinction to the discontinuity of the state q [printed p. 7, Section 1.4, final paragraph; printed p. 8, selected sentence]."
    ],
    "implicit_context": [
      "The selected passage occurs in the discussion of linear waves in discontinuous media [printed pp. 7–8, Section 1.4, title and material-interface discussion].",
      "Finite volume cells may be assigned different material properties by averaging material parameters over each cell; this motivates the interface setting [printed p. 8, Section 1.4, first paragraph, sentence preceding the selected sentence].",
      "Neighboring cell averages can supply the two initial states, but this is an application of the Riemann problem rather than part of its general definition [printed p. 5, Section 1.2.1, paragraph following equation (1.11)].",
      "Conservation form is not a standing requirement for the variable-coefficient setting discussed here [printed p. 8, Section 1.4, second paragraph]."
    ],
